<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee of the Board and were approved by the Board of Directors at its meeting held on 10th February, 2021 and have been subjected to Limited Review by the Statutory Auditors.  n2. The company operates under one segment of Kitchen &amp; Home appliances.  n3. These Financial Results have been prepared in accordance with the Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015 (Ind AS) prescribed under Sec 133 of the Companies Act, 2013.  n4. The Figure shown  under  Other Comprehensive Income   in consolidated Financials, includes , Effect of Changes in Foreign Exchange Rates arising on account of restatement of Assets and Liabilities of the subsidiary in INR.  n5. The Company has choosen to exercise the option permitted under Sec.115BAA of the Income Tax Act 1961. Accordingly, the Company has recognised Provision for Current Tax and Deffered Tax at the rates prescribed in this section.  n6. In early Dec 2020, the Company's wholly owned stepdown subsidiary, Horwood Homewares Limited UK, divested its 51% stake in Horwood Life Limted, UK and the loss of Rs. 6.11 crores arising out of this discountinued operation is reported under the head 'Loss from discontinued operations'.  n7. The code of Social Security 2020(Code) which received the Presidential Assent, subsumes nine laws relating to social security, retirement and employee benefits, including the Employees Provident Fund and Miscellaneious Provisions Act, 1952 and the Payment of Gratuity Act, 1972.  The effetive date of the code is yet to be notified and related rules are yet to be defined.  The impact of the changes, if any, will be assessed and recognized post notification of the relevant provisions  n8. The Investors can visit the company's website www.ttkprestige.com for updated information</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
